# Gradle properties — only the user-level one, which is where credentials go.
# This pattern used to be unanchored, so it also swallowed every *project's*
# gradle.properties. That is build configuration, not secrets: the Android test
# rig needs `android.useAndroidX=true` there, so with the file ignored the rig
# could not be configured at all from a clean checkout. Nobody noticed because
# the file existed on the machine that wrote it.
/gradle.properties


# Omnivore coverage artifacts (execution data, probe maps, instrumentation stats)
*.omnivore
*.probes
*.stats
